          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*3. How many three-digit numbers are divisible by 7? ("
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " All three-digit numbers divisible by 7 form an AP. Find the smallest and largest such three-digit numbers.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.169,
            0.886,
            0.229
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*4. How many multiples of 4 lie between 10 and 250? ("
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hint:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " All multiples of 4 form an AP. Find the smallest and largest multiples of 4 between 10 and 250.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.233,
            0.885,
            0.273
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*5. Find a GP for which the sum of the first two terms is – 4 and the fifth term is 4 times the third term."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.276,
            0.885,
            0.315
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*6. Find all possible ways of expressing 100 as the sum of consecutive natural numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.321,
            0.887,
            0.407
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*7. The number of bacteria in a certain culture doubles every hour. If there were 30 bacteria present in the culture originally, how many bacteria will be present at the end of the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 ^ { \\mathrm { n d } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " hour, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " hour and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " hour?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.412,
            0.884,
            0.452
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*8. The sum of the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "8 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " terms of an AP is 24 and the sum of the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " terms is 44. Find the first three terms of the AP."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.455,
            0.884,
            0.496
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*9. Find the smallest value of n such that the sum of the first n natural numbers is greater than 1,000."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.498,
            0.885,
            0.539
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*10. Which term of the GP: 2, 8, 32, … is 131072? Write the explicit formula as well as the recursive formula for the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { t h }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " term."
