          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.66,
            0.884,
            0.7
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*13. The sum of the first three terms of a geometric progression is 26, and the sum of their squares is 364. Find the terms of the GP."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.702,
            0.885,
            0.769
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*14. Suppose "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "P_{1}=1,P_{2}=2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n > 2, P_{n} = P_{1} + P_{2} + \\cdots + P_{n - 1} + 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Find the values of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{P}_{1}, \\mathrm{P}_{2}, \\ldots, \\mathrm{P}_{8}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Can you find a simpler recursive formula for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { { P _ { n } } } ^ { \\mathrm { { \\scriptsize ~ \\hat { \\prime } } } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Can you give an explicit formula?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.772,
            0.885,
            0.839
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*15. Suppose "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "W_{1} = 1,\\ W_{2} = 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n > 2,\\; \\mathrm{W}_{n} = \\mathrm{W}_{1} + \\mathrm{W}_{2} + \\cdots +"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "W _ { \\mathrm { n - 2 } } + 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Find the values of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathsf{W}_{1}, \\mathsf{W}_{2}, \\ldots, \\mathsf{W}_{8}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Do you recognise this sequence?"
            }
          ]
        }
